{"name":"Urban Legend","hex":"#67585f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"urban legend","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A widely circulated story that is untrue or dubious, often having elements of humor or horror."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/urban_legend"}],"entries":[{"title":"Urban legend","blocks":[{"text":"An urban legend is a form of folklore consisting of unusual, humorous, or frightening stories that circulate as true accounts but are typically unverified or apocryphal. These narratives are often shared through word of mouth, social media, or news-like sources and typically involve shocking, mysterious, or cautionary themes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Bunnyman_bridge_night.jpg/330px-Bunnyman_bridge_night.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Urban_legend"},{"title":"Urban Legend (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Urban Legend is a 1998 slasher film directed by Jamie Blanks, written by Silvio Horta, and starring Jared Leto, Alicia Witt, Rebecca Gayheart, Tara Reid, and Michael Rosenbaum, and is the first installment in the Urban Legend film series. Its plot focuses on a series of murders on the campus of a private New England university, all of which appear to be modeled after popular urban legends. In addition to its core cast, the film features supporting performances from Robert Englund, Joshua Jackson, Danielle Harris, Loretta Devine, John Neville, Natasha Gregson Wagner, and Brad Dourif. It is an international co-production between the United States, Canada and France."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/56/Urban_Legend_film.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Urban_Legend_(film)"},{"title":"Legend","blocks":[{"text":"A legend is a genre of folklore that consists of a narrative featuring human actions, believed or perceived to have taken place in human history. Narratives in this genre may demonstrate human values, and possess certain qualities that give the tale verisimilitude. Legend, for its active and passive participants, may include miracles. Legends may be transformed over time to keep them fresh and vital."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/John_Collier_-_Lady_Godiva_-_c_1898_-_Herbert_Art_Gallery_and_Museum.jpg/330px-John_Collier_-_Lady_Godiva_-_c_1898_-_Herbert_Art_Gallery_and_Museum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Legend"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Silverpilen_vid_kymlinge_sp%C3%B6kstation.png/500px-Silverpilen_vid_kymlinge_sp%C3%B6kstation.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Silverpilen_vid_kymlinge_sp%C3%B6kstation.png/500px-Silverpilen_vid_kymlinge_sp%C3%B6kstation.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An example of a supposed ghost train, the Silver Train of Stockholm, also known as Silverpilen (the Silver Arrow), artist's impression","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASilverpilen_vid_kymlinge_sp%C3%B6kstation.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Toronto_-_ON_-_Hart_House.jpg/500px-Toronto_-_ON_-_Hart_House.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Toronto_-_ON_-_Hart_House.jpg/1280px-Toronto_-_ON_-_Hart_House.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Toronto_-_ON_-_Hart_House.jpg/500px-Toronto_-_ON_-_Hart_House.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"T